  <preface>
    <title>Introduction</title>
    <p>
      This book has been written for use in Walla Walla University's Math 105, <em>Math for the Liberal Arts</em> class (previously titled <em>Finite Mathematics</em>). This course is taught over a 10-week quarter and fulfills the general studies mathematics requirement for many non-STEM majors. During a 10-week term I typically cover all sections except 1.5 (Income Taxes), 2.5 (Logical Fallacies), and 3.7 (Expected Value). These sections are included for colleagues who cover the material differently.
    </p>
  </preface>

